    <div class="surface-bento calc-strategy-card">
      <div class="score-header-split">
        <h2 class="text-widget-title">The 3-Point Field Test for Aircraft Noise</h2>
        <span class="text-overline text-accent-alpine">Advisor Perspective</span>
      </div>
      <p class="text-body section-body-prose">
        Don't rely on a 10-minute Sunday open house visit to judge aircraft noise. Regional flight tracks shift between North Flow and South Flow depending on wind and weather patterns. I recommend a 3-point field test: stand outside in the yard for 20 minutes during peak morning or evening departure windows, inspect the windows to see if acoustic double-pane or triple-pane retrofits are installed, and check if the home falls inside an official airport sound insulation grant boundary. In addition, installing high-efficiency MERV 13 or HEPA HVAC air filtration easily mitigates low-altitude jet fuel ultrafine particles (UFPs).
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

