  <section class="content-section-centered">
    <h2 class="text-section-title">Airfield Operations &amp; Environmental Protection</h2>
    <div class="section-grid-static grid-cols-2">
      
      <article class="surface-bento calc-strategy-card">
        <header class="text-center">
          <div class="text-overline text-accent-alpine">24/7 Logistics Operations</div>
          <h3 class="text-widget-title">Air Cargo &amp; Freight Corridors</h3>
        </header>
        <p class="text-body">
          While Sea-Tac handles passenger volume, Boeing Field operates 24/7 as a premier cargo hub. Major logistics carriers like UPS, DHL, and Amazon Air operate heavy jet freighters out of KBFI, frequently running late-night and early-morning departure schedules over the Duwamish River valley.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="surface-bento calc-strategy-card">
        <header class="text-center">
          <div class="text-overline text-accent-alpine">Aviation Manufacturing</div>
          <h3 class="text-widget-title">Boeing Flight Testing</h3>
        </header>
        <p class="text-body">
          Both Paine Field (Everett) and Boeing Field (Seattle) support active flight testing. Boeing conducts initial widebody assembly testing, military aircraft transport (such as KC-46 tankers and P-8 Poseidons), and customer delivery flights directly over surrounding residential hillsides.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="surface-bento calc-strategy-card">
        <header class="text-center">
          <div class="text-overline text-accent-alpine">Noise Mitigation</div>
          <h3 class="text-widget-title">Airport Sound Insulation Programs</h3>
        </header>
        <p class="text-body">
          The Port of Seattle and regional airport authorities have funded extensive acoustic insulation programs for homes inside official 65 dB DNL noise contours. Upgrades include triple-pane acoustic windows, solid-core exterior doors, and enhanced attic insulation buffering.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="surface-bento calc-strategy-card">
        <header class="text-center">
          <div class="text-overline text-accent-alpine">Air Quality Defense</div>
          <h3 class="text-widget-title">Ultrafine Particles (UFPs)</h3>
        </header>
        <p class="text-body">
          Aircraft engines release microscopic ultrafine combustion particles during low-altitude takeoff and landing. Using MERV 13 furnace filters or installing standalone HEPA air purifiers inside the home effectively traps airborne aviation particulates.
        </p>
      </article>

    </div>
  </section>

